DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions return the value associated with a DWARF attribute de‐
     scribing a constant.

     Function ddwwaarrff__ffoorrmmuuddaattaa() sets the location pointed to by argument _r_e_t
     to the value of the attribute referenced by argument _a_t_t_r, treating the
     value as an unsigned quantity.  Argument _a_t_t_r must have one of the fol‐
     lowing forms: DW_FORM_data1, DW_FORM_data2, DW_FORM_data4, DW_FORM_data8
     and DW_FORM_udata.

     Function ddwwaarrff__ffoorrmmssddaattaa() sets the location pointed to by argument _r_e_t
     to the value of the attribute referenced by argument _a_t_t_r, appropriately
     sign extended.  Argument _a_t_t_r must have one of the following forms:
     DW_FORM_data1, DW_FORM_data2, DW_FORM_data4, DW_FORM_data8 and
     DW_FORM_sdata.

     If argument _e_r_r is not NULL, it will be used to return an error descrip‐
     tor in case of an error.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     These functions return DW_DLV_OK on success.  In case of an error, they
     return DW_DLV_ERROR and set argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     These functions may fail with the following errors:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]       Either of arguments _a_t_t_r or _r_e_t was NULL.

     [DW_DLE_ATTR_FORM_BAD]  The attribute referenced by argument _a_t_t_r was not
                             of a permitted kind.

